@title Webhook delivery
@subtitle Parcelwise integrations docs, version dated 2026-10-05

## Delivery sequence
!! A response slower than 10 seconds counts as a failure, and the event is retried.

diagram hook sequence title="Webhook delivery"
hook: order "Order Service" svc
hook: bus "Event Bus" queue
hook: worker "Delivery Worker" fn
hook: merch "Merchant Endpoint" ext
hook: dlq "Dead Letter Queue" queue
hook: order -> bus : publish order.shipped
hook: bus -> worker : deliver event
hook: worker -> merch : POST /webhooks, signed, 10 s timeout
hook: merch --> worker : 503 Service Unavailable
hook: worker -> bus : requeue with 1 minute delay
hook: bus -> worker : deliver event, attempt 2
hook: worker -> merch : POST /webhooks
hook: merch --> worker : 200 OK
hook: worker -> bus : acknowledge
hook: opt "merchant never recovers"
hook: worker -> dlq : park after attempt 6
hook: end

## Retry schedule
table = attempt,delay after previous failure; 1,immediate; 2,1 minute; 3,5 minutes; 4,30 minutes; 5,2 hours; 6,12 hours

## Good to know
- Every request carries an X-Parcelwise-Signature header, which is the HMAC-SHA256 of the body.
- Events can arrive out of order, so merchants should compare the sequence number.
- Parked events are kept for 14 days and can be replayed from the dashboard.
